# jemdoc: menu{MENU}{pub.html}, nofooter
== Publications

\* means equal contributions.

# Like *bold* and /italic/, _underscore_ can be used for emphasis in this modified version of +jemdoc+.  Useful for highlighting different parts of a bibliography item as:

=== Conference papers
. \[*WAFR'24*\] _Dongjie Yu\*_, Hang Xu\*, Yizhou Chen, Yi Ren and Jia Pan. "BiKC: Keypose-Conditioned Consistency Policy for Bimanual Robotic Manipulatio". In /The 16th International Workshop on the Algorithmic Foundations of Robotics/, 2024.
.. tldr: We present Bimanual Keypose-Conditioned Consistency Policy (BiKC) to enhance the operational reliability and eﬃciency by overcoming per-stage error and per-step latency accumulated across multiple stages.
.. [https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.10093 \[Paper\]] [https://github.com/manUtdMoon/bikc \[Code\]]
#
. \[*ICML'22*\] _Dongjie Yu\*_, Haitong Ma\*, Shengbo Eben Li and Jianyu Chen. "Reachability Constrained Reinforcement Learning". In /Proceedings of the 39th International Conference on Machine Learning/, PMLR 162:25636-25655, 2022.
.. tldr: We characterize feasible sets (persistently safe states) with Hamilton-Jacobi reachability analysis in constrained RL. The algorithm reachs a zero-violation policy with competitive performance.
.. [https://proceedings.mlr.press/v162/yu22d.html \[Paper\]] [https://github.com/mahaitongdae/Reachability_Constrained_RL \[Code\_learning\]] [https://github.com/ManUtdMoon/safe-control-gym \[Code\_env\]]

=== Journal papers
. \[*T-ASE*\] Hang Xu, Yizhou Chen, _Dongjie Yu_, Yi Ren and Jia Pan. "BiKC+: Bimanual Hierarchical Imitation with Keypose-Conditioned Coordination-Aware Consistency Policies". /IEEE Transactions on Automation Science and Engineering/, DOI: 10.1109/TASE.2025.3639130, 2025.
.. tldr: We use a VLM to autonomously identify contact mode to optionally merge bimanual keyposes, thus enabling coordination-aware bimanual manipulation.
.. [https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/11271705 \[Paper\]] [https://github.com/JoanaHXU/BiKC-plus/ \[Code\]]
#
. \[*T-ASE*\] _Dongjie Yu_, Wenjun Zou, Yujie Yang, Haitong Ma, Shengbo Eben Li, Yuming Yin, Jianyu Chen and Jingliang Duan. "Safe Model-Based Reinforcement Learning with an Uncertainty-Aware Reachability Certificate". /IEEE Transactions on Automation Science and Engineering/, DOI: 10.1109/TASE.2023.3292388, 2023.
.. tldr: We propose a distributional form of reachability certificate to consider the uncertaity of the system dynamics in safe RL. The algorithm is able to learn a zero-violation policy with competitive performance, significantly reducing violations during exploration.
.. [https://ieeexplore.ieee.org/document/10329343 \[Paper\]] [https://github.com/ManUtdMoon/Distributional-Reachability-Policy-Optimization \[Code\]]

=== Preprints
. _Dongjie Yu\*_, Kun Lei\*, Zhennan Jiang, Jia Pan and Huazhe Xu. "Beyond Action Residuals: Real-World Robot Policy Steering via Bottleneck Latent Reinforcement Learning", arXiv preprint 2605.19919, 2026.
.. tldr: We propose Z-Perturbation Reinforcement Learning (ZPRL), an RL finetuning framework that steers pretrained robot policies by perturbing bottleneck latents, improving sample efficiency and real-world manipulation performance while producing smoother actions than action residuals.
.. [https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.19919 \[Paper\]] [https://github.com/manUtdMoon/ZPRL \[Code\]]
#
. Kun Lei\*, Huanyu Li\*, _Dongjie Yu\*_, Zhenyu Wei, Lingxiao Guo, Zhennan Jiang, Ziyu Wang, Shiyu Liang and Huazhe Xu. "RL-100: Performant Robotic Manipulation with Real-World Reinforcement Learning", arXiv preprint 2510.14830, 2025.
.. tldr: We introduce RL-100, a real-world RL system consisting of imitation, iterative offline and online RL. RL-100 achieves 100% success rate on eight diverse real-world tasks, demonstrating the potential of real-world RL for deployable robotic manipulation.
.. [https://arxiv.org/abs/2510.14830 \[Paper\]]

